<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows at $80.5 mln March 18.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows at $80.5 mln March 18.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $80.5 million deficit on March 18 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data supplied to banks.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON MARCH 18</p>
<p>Exports: $190.9 million</p>
<p>Imports: $238.1 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $125.7 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $159 million</p>
<p>Deficit: $80.5 million</p>
<p>MARCH DOLLAR FLOWS UP TO DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $2.487 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $2.222 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $2.864 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $2.395 billion</p>
<p>Net surplus: $734 million</p>
<p>Note: the figures were rounded off.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 2485415))</p>
</text>
